@startuml
actor "User" as User
participant ":Topic Modelling Step\n(Frontend, subStep \"generated\")" as UI
participant ":PipelineStore\n(Zustand)" as Store

autonumber

== Preconditions ==
note over User, UI
  User is authenticated, a project is active, and topic generation
  has completed (topicSubStep = "generated"). All editing here is
  frontend-only: nothing is written to the backend until the user
  triggers reconciliation or training with the current list.
end note

== Display ==

UI -> Store : Read generatedTopics
Store --> UI : list[Topic]
UI --> User : Display numbered topic cards\n("N topics generated", name + description, checkbox per card)

== Optional: Edit Topic (inline) ==

opt User edits a topic
    User -> UI : Click pencil -> change name and/or description
    note over UI : Confirm (check) is disabled until BOTH\nname and description are non-empty
    User -> UI : Confirm edit
    UI -> Store : updateGeneratedTopic(topic_id, name, description)
    Store --> UI : Updated generatedTopics
    UI --> User : Reflect changes inline
end

== Optional: Delete Topic ==

opt User deletes a topic
    User -> UI : Click trash icon
    UI --> User : Confirmation modal\n("\"<name>\" will be removed. This cannot be undone.")
    alt User confirms
        User -> UI : Confirm delete
        UI -> Store : deleteGeneratedTopic(topic_id)
        Store --> UI : Reduced generatedTopics\n(plain removal — deleting to an empty list is allowed)
        UI --> User : Reflect updated topic list
    else User cancels
        UI --> User : Modal dismissed, no change
    end
end

== Optional: Merge Topics (frontend-only) ==

opt User merges topics
    User -> UI : Select topics via checkboxes
    note over UI : "Merge Selected" is disabled until >= 2 are checked
    User -> UI : Open Merge dialog
    UI --> User : Dialog pre-filled\n(name = constituents joined by " + ",\ndescription = first selected topic's description)
    note over UI : "Merge Topics" is disabled until BOTH\nname and description are non-empty
    alt User confirms
        User -> UI : Provide/adjust name + description, confirm
        UI -> Store : mergeGeneratedTopics(selected_ids, name, description)
        note right of Store
          Creates a new Topic with a fresh UUID and
          origin_topic_ids = union of the constituents'
          generation ids (origin_topic_ids, or own id if none).
          The originals are removed; the merged topic is appended.
        end note
        Store --> UI : Updated generatedTopics
        UI --> User : Display list with the merged topic in place
    else User cancels
        UI --> User : Dialog dismissed, no change
    end
end

== Proceed (no backend call here) ==

note over User, UI
  There is no separate "accept / validate" action. From step 2b the
  user proceeds via one of two buttons, BOTH disabled while the list
  is empty (the only "at least one topic" enforcement):
    - "Reconcile Topics"   -> dispatches reconciliation (see UC 1.4)
    - "Skip to Labelling -> " -> setStep("label") with the current list
  The current (edited/merged) generatedTopics is the list carried forward.
end note

@enduml
